4758	REG-1741205601873	Occupational Safety and Health Administration Regulation 2024-001	Workplace Safety Standards	Occupational Safety and Health Act of 1970		This regulation outlines enhanced safety protocols and standards to address emerging hazards in modern workplaces. It aims to ensure a safer working environment across various industries by incorporating advancements in safety technology and updated scientific research. The regulation covers aspects such as the use and maintenance of protective equipment, emergency preparedness, and the implementation of safety management systems.	Employers must conduct regular safety audits, provide necessary training to employees for equipment operation and emergency procedures, maintain updated records of workplace incidents, and ensure that all protective equipment meets specified federal standards. Compliance includes integrating an ergonomics assessment program and adopting new technologies to monitor and mitigate potential risks.	Campus Safety	federal	t	\N	\N	2025-06-05 14:29:40.704	2025-03-05 20:13:21.873	2026-03-05 20:13:21.873	\N		https://www.osha.gov	Occupational Safety and Health Administration		U.S. Department of Labor					\N		\N	\N			\N	\N	1	\N	2025-03-07 15:21:09.709673	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "agency_submission", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}]		\N	\N
