4817	REG-1741278195600	Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972; a Policy Interpretation; Title IX and Intercollegiate Athletics	Civil Rights	45 CFR Part 86		The regulation interprets Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, prohibiting sex discrimination in educational programs receiving federal assistance. It provides guidelines for compliance in intercollegiate athletics, including financial assistance, program areas, and meeting the interests and abilities of male and female students.	1. Compliance in Financial Assistance: Financial aid should be available proportionately to male and female participants. 2. Compliance in Other Program Areas: Male and female athletes should receive equivalent treatment, benefits, and opportunities. 3. Compliance in Meeting the Interests and Abilities of Male and Female Students: Athletic interests and abilities of male and female students must be equally accommodated.	Civil Rights	federal	t	\N	\N	2025-03-06 16:23:15.6	2025-03-06 16:23:15.6	2026-03-06 16:23:15.6	\N		https://www.ed.gov/about/offices/list/ocr/docs/t9interp.html#skipnav2	U.S. Department of Education		Office for Civil Rights					\N		\N	\N			\N	\N	1	\N	2025-03-07 15:21:09.709673	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "agency_submission", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}]		\N	\N
