4709	REG1923	Worker Adjustment and Retraining Notification Act (WARN)	Recruitment Hiring & Termination			The University must provide 60 days advance notice of plant closings or mass layoffs to affected workers (whether hourly or salaried, including managers or supervisors) or their representatives (i.e. labor union).\r\n\r\n \tNotice also must be given to the state dislocated worker unit and the appropriate unit of local government.\r\n\r\n \tFailure to comply may result in liability to each aggrieved employee for back pay and benefits for the period of violation up to 60 days, and $500 for each day of violation for failing to notify the unit of local govt.		Human Resources	federal	t	\N	\N	2014-01-26 00:00:00	\N	\N	\N		https://www.dol.gov	Department of Labor									\N	\N			\N	\N	1	\N	2025-03-07 15:21:09.709673	\N	t	\N	\N	\N	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "agency_submission", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}]		\N	\N
