4711	REG1954	Animal Welfare Act	Research	7 U.S.C. §§ 2131-2159	1731	Governs the treatment of animals used for research: dogs, cats, monkeys, guinea pigs, hamsters, and other warm-blooded animals.\n\nAdditional Information:\nGoverns the treatment of animals used for research: dogs, cats, monkeys, guinea pigs, hamsters, and other warm-blooded animals.	9 C.F.R. § 2.36: Each reporting facility shall submit an annual report to the AC Regional Director for the State where the facility is located on or before December 1 of each calendar year. AC Regional Director means a veterinarian or his designee, employed by the U.S. Department of Agriculture Animal and Plant Health Inspection Service (APHIS), who is assigned by the Administrator to supervise and perform the official work of APHIS in a given state or states.\n\nAdditional Requirements:\n9 C.F.R. § 2.36: Each reporting facility shall submit an annual report to the AC Regional Director for the State where the facility is located on or before December 1 of each calendar year. AC Regional Director means a veterinarian or his designee, employed by the U.S. Department of Agriculture Animal and Plant Health Inspection Service (APHIS), who is assigned by the Administrator to supervise and perform the official work of APHIS in a given state or states.	Research	federal	t	\N	\N	2025-03-06 14:30:42.93	\N	\N	\N	9 C.F.R. § 2.36: Each reporting facility shall submit an annual report to the AC Regional Director for the State where the facility is located on or before December 1 of each calendar year. AC Regional Director means a veterinarian or his designee, employed by the U.S. Department of Agriculture Animal and Plant Health Inspection Service (APHIS), who is assigned by the Administrator to supervise and perform the official work of APHIS in a given state or states.	\N	\N							9 C.F.R. § 2.36: Each reporting facility shall submit an annual report to the AC Regional Director for the State where the facility is located on or before