4840	PA-paCHE-1741801720622	Pennsylvania Department of Education (PDE)	Higher Education		\N	The Pennsylvania Department of Education (PDE) oversees 500 public school districts, more than 170 public charter schools, public cyber charter schools, Career and Technology Centers/Vocational Technical schools, public Intermediate Units, the education of youth in State Juvenile Correctional Institutions, Head Starts and publicly funded preschools, and community colleges.\nPDE also oversees policies related to public, academic, and school libraries, and the State Library of Pennsylvania.\nClearan	The Pennsylvania Department of Education (PDE) oversees 500 public school districts, more than 170 public charter schools, public cyber charter schools, Career and Technology Centers/Vocational Technical schools, public Intermediate Units, the education of youth in State Juvenile Correctional Institutions, Head Starts and publicly funded preschools, and community colleges.\nPDE also oversees policies related to public, academic, and school libraries, and the State Library of Pennsylvania.\nClearances & Background Checks\nContinuing Education and Professional Development\nChild Labor Laws\nSpecial Education\nCertification Testing Requirements\nAccessibility\nTranscripts & Diplomas\n2024-25 Education Budget\nState Board of Higher Education to Embark on Statewide Stakeholder Engagement Tour to Help Develop Strategic Plan\nShapiro Administration Highlights Commonsense Investments to Fight Food Insecurity at Millersville University\nShapiro Administration Invites Nominations for National RISE Award to Honor Exceptional School Employees Across Pennsylvania\nShapiro Administration Announces $300,000 to Educate Students Recovering at Home from Serious Medical Conditions\nContact Us Form\nContact by Phone\nPDE Executive Staff\nPDE Press Office\nState Library of Pennsylvania\nCollecting, preserving, and providing access to materials for, by, and about Pennsylvania.\nProfessional Standards and Practices Commission\nThe Professional Standards and Practices Commission sets preparation, certification, practice, and conduct standards for teachers.\nState Board of Education\nThe State Board of Education reviews, develops, and adopts regulations that govern basic and higher education in the Commonwealth.\nState Board of Higher Education\nProvide direction, coordination, and support to ensure that institutions of higher education fully meet the workforce and economic development needs of this Commonwealth.\n	Campus Safety	state	t	\N	\N	2025-03-12 19:09:15.595	2025-03-12 19:08:35.19	\N	\N	\N	https://www.education.pa.gov/Postsecondary-Adult/College%20and%20Career%20Education/Pages/default.aspx	paCHE	\N	paCHE	https://www.education.pa.gov/agencies/education.html	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	[{"url": "https://www.education.pa.gov/agencies/education.html", "type": "web-scrape", "lastChecked": "2025-03-12T19:08:35.190Z"}]	23	4840	2025-03-12 17:48:42.231851	\N	t	\N	PA	paCHE	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "agency_submission", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}]		\N	\N
4844	PA-paHigherEd-1741802622301	Certification Testing Requirements	Higher Education		\N	Pennsylvania Department of Education (PDE)\nOverview\nThe Pennsylvania Department of Education (PDE) oversees 500 public school districts, more than 170 public charter schools, public cyber charter schools, Career and Technology Centers/Vocational Technical schools, public Intermediate Units, the education of youth in State Juvenile Correctional Institutions, Head Starts and publicly funded preschools, and community colleges.\nPDE also oversees policies related to public, academic, and school libra	Pennsylvania Department of Education (PDE)\nOverview\nThe Pennsylvania Department of Education (PDE) oversees 500 public school districts, more than 170 public charter schools, public cyber charter schools, Career and Technology Centers/Vocational Technical schools, public Intermediate Units, the education of youth in State Juvenile Correctional Institutions, Head Starts and publicly funded preschools, and community colleges.\nPDE also oversees policies related to public, academic, and school libraries, and the State Library of Pennsylvania.\nCertification\nLogin to TIMS\n•\nClearances & Background Checks\n•\nContinuing Education and Professional Development\n•\nChild Labor Laws\n•\nSpecial Education\n•\nCertification Testing Requirements\n•\nAccessibility\n•\nTranscripts & Diplomas\n•\n2024-25 Education Budget\nTeach in PA\nEmpowerU\nFood & Nutrition\nCareer and Technical Education\nNew Releases\n•\nState Board of Higher Education to Embark on Statewide Stakeholder Engagement Tour to Help Develop Strategic Plan\n•\nShapiro Administration Highlights Commonsense Investments to Fight Food Insecurity at Millersville University\n•\nShapiro Administration Invites Nominations for National RISE Award to Honor Exceptional School Employees Across Pennsylvania\n•\nShapiro Administration Announces $300,000 to Educate Students Recovering at Home from Serious Medical Conditions\nContact Information & Affiliates\n•\nContact Us Form\n•\nContact by Phone\n•\nPDE Executive Staff\n•\nPDE Press Office\n•\nState Library of Pennsylvania\nCollecting, preserving, and providing access to materials for, by, and about Pennsylvania.\n•\nProfessional Standards and Practices Commission\nThe Professional Standards and Practices Commission sets preparation, certification, practice, and conduct standards for teachers.\n•\nState Board of Education\nThe State Board of Education reviews, develops, and adopts regulations that govern basic and higher education in the Commonwealth.\n•\nState Board of Higher Education\nProvide direction, coordination, and support to ensure that institutions of higher education fully meet the workforce and economic development needs of this Commonwealth.	Academic Programs	state	t	\N	\N	2025-03-12 18:41:17.121	2025-03-12 18:40:49.246	\N	\N	\N	https://www.education.pa.gov/Postsecondary-Adult/Pages/default.aspx	paHigherEd	\N	paHigherEd	https://www.education.pa.gov/social-media-policy-and-disclaimer.html	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	[{"url": "https://www.education.pa.gov/social-media-policy-and-disclaimer.html", "type": "web-scrape", "lastChecked": "2025-03-12T18:40:49.246Z"}]	19	4844	2025-03-12 18:03:42.335663	\N	t	\N	PA	paHigherEd	[{"type": "attestation", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "website_publish", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "community_communication", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}, {"type": "agency_submission", "status": "pending", "enabled": true, "required": false}]		\N	\N
