4830	2025-03-12 18:05:08.544	16	6	1	119433d7173a	compliance-app	3764	CONTENT_TITLE_EXTRACTION	{"_level": "INFO", "_facility": "LOCAL0", "_timestamp": "2025-03-12T18:05:08.544Z", "extractedTitle": "", "firstParagraph": "Department of Environmental Protection\\nOur mission is to protect Pennsylvania’s air, land, and water resources while ensuring the health and safety of all residents and visitors to the commonwealth.\\nSubmit an incident or complaint\\nStreamlining Permits for Economic Expansion and Development (SPEED)\\nCreated to accelerate permit processing and keep Pennsylvania aligned with business demands, eligible permit applications will use DEP-approved contractors for expedited review.\\nThe Invitation For Bids (IFB) is now open to find qualified professionals to fill these roles.\\nRead more about SPEED\\nPopular\\nFalcon Cam\\nFlooding and Storm Resources\\nEnvironmental Justice\\nEnergy Programs Office\\nLearn more about\\nClimate Change\\nPennsylvania Pipeline Portal\\nPFAS in Pennsylvania\\nDriving PA Forward\\nMethane Reduction Strategy\\nStormwater Management\\nBay Restoration\\nLead in Drinking Water\\nMine Subsidence Insurance\\nThe Environmental Regulatory Process in Pennsylvania\\nStream Maintenance\\nNews releases\\nReview all press releases\\nDEP to Host Public Hearing on North Centre Township HSCA Investigation in Columbia County\\nDEP Provides Update on Lancaster County Plane Crash Cleanup\\nShapiro Administration Holds Energy Transfer Accountable for Contaminating\\nShapiro Administration Launches RISE PA Initiative to Create Energy Jobs, Cut Costs, Grow Pennsylvania’s Energy & Manufacturing Industries, and Lower Toxic Air Pollution\\nRISE PA will create thousands of good-paying jobs in construction and manufacturing – the $396 million program is for projects to reduce energy costs and air pollution from industrial facilities.\\nUnion labor, environmental advocates, and leaders from across the energy industry have praised the Shapiro Administration’s commonsense efforts to create jobs and tackle industrial pollution while helping build healthier communities and a stronger economy in Pennsylvania.\\nAccessibility and discrimination\\nThe Pennsylvania Department of Environmental Protection (DEP) works to make sure everyone can access its services. Learn more about how we do this by reading our policy.\\nPAyback\\nEligible for a refund of your permits, licenses, or certification application fees?​\\nCheck Now\\nJosh Shapiro, Governor\\nJessica Shirley, Acting Secretary\\nDepartment of Environmental Protection social contacts Follow on Facebook\\nDepartment of Environmental Protection social contacts Follow on X\\nDepartment of Environmental Protection social contacts Follow on LinkedIn\\nDepartment of Environmental Protection social contacts Follow on Instagram\\nDepartment of Environmental Protection social contacts Follow on YouTube\\nDepartment of Environmental Protection social contacts Contact Us\\nMedia Inquiries\\nOpen Data Portal"}	Content-based title extraction result
